  "final_message": "I've run `git status` in `orders-service` and will check the output once it completes.\nI've started running the test suite in `orders-service` to establish our baseline.\nI've initiated a search across repositories to see how `OrderPlaced` is consumed.\nI'm checking whether `analytics-ingest` references `channel`.\nI'm checking whether `web-storefront` references `channel`.\nI'll check the recent commit logs for context.\nI'll check the git log in `analytics-ingest`.\nI'm running the tests in `analytics-ingest` to verify its existing contract tests.\nI'll wait for the test run in `analytics-ingest` to finish.\nI'm checking the workspace directory structure.\nI'm checking `C:\\avg` for context.\n`channel` cannot be dropped from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the order model because **`analytics-ingest` (team Data) actively depends on it**.\n\n### Evidence in `analytics-ingest`\n\n1. **Contract Requirement**:\n   According to the [contract documentation](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/README.md#L26-L32), `OrderPlaced` requires `channel` (`web|store|marketplace`), and missing fields cause ingestion to reject with [`ContractViolationError`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/errors.ts#L5-L10).\n\n2. **Schema & Decoding**:\n   In [`decodeOrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts#L22-L29), the event reader explicitly validates `channel`:\n   ```ts\n   const channel = reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS);\n   ```\n\n3. **Data Lake Storage**:\n   In [`toOrderRow`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts#L48-L56), `channel` is populated directly into the data lake `orders` table:\n   ```ts\n   export function toOrderRow(event: OrderPlacedEvent): OrderRow {\n     return {\n       order_id: event.orderId,\n       placed_date: toDateString(event.placedAt),\n       channel: event.channel,\n       currency: event.currency,\n       units: totalUnits(event.lines),\n     };\n   }\n   ```\n\n4. **Contract Enforcement Tests**:\n   [`test/ingest.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts#L52-L58) has contract verification tests (`requires channel` and `rejects an unknown channel`) that will fail if `channel` is missing.\n\n### Impact\n\nRemoving `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in [`orders-service`](file:///C:/avg/w2/r/orders-service/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) would break downstream ingestion for team Data, rejecting all incoming `OrderPlaced` events.\n\nBefore dropping `channel` from `orders-service`, team Data must first update `analytics-ingest` to remove its dependency on `channel` (or make the field optional in the ingestion contract).\n",
